<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold Louis, Count Palatine of Veldenz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1625–1694</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold Louis was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of Veldenz, ruling the small principality from 1634 to 1694. His lands suffered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and the French wars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>. He died without surviving sons, and the inheritance was disputed among the Palatine branches for decades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-louis-count-palatine-of-veldenz.jpg" alt="Leopold Louis, Count Palatine of Veldenz" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_Louis_of_Palatinate-Veldenz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
